<!-- TEMPLATE. This is the canonical shape of a UPS Wire article. It is the
     file to hand a Claude Artifact session as "match this structure".

     It is NOT itself renderable: the two placeholder comments below are
     substituted at build time. Everything else here ships as-is.

     WHY A FULL DOCUMENT, not a fragment: an article has to render in three
     places from one file -- inside MFL (fetched, spliced, srcdoc'd by
     site/wire/mfl_hpm_embed_loader.js), at its own public GitHub Pages URL,
     and pasted into a Claude Artifact. Only a complete self-contained
     document does all three. That is also why the CSS is inlined rather than
     <link>ed: an Artifact has no network access.

     THE FOUR HARD RULES (site/wire/README.md):
       1. No href="#..." anywhere. Inside a srcdoc document with a <base>, a
          fragment link resolves against the base and navigates the frame to
          jsDelivr, which serves it as text/plain -- the article turns into a
          wall of source code. Use <button> + data attributes.
       2. No vh/svh/dvh units. In an auto-sized iframe 100vh equals the height
          we just set, so the frame grows every beacon tick. vw is fine.
       3. No &lt;script type="application/json">. check_inline_js.mjs runs
          node --check on EVERY inline script regardless of type, and a
          top-level JSON object is a SyntaxError.
       4. No webfonts. System stack only -- a CDN <link> breaks in Artifacts.
-->

<style data-wire-style="tokens+article" data-wire-style-sha="sha256-PLACEHOLDER">
<!--WIRE_STYLE-->
</style>
